@page "/"
@using Slip39Demo.UI.Shared

<PageTitle>SLIP-39 + age wallet backup</PageTitle>

<h1 class="with-icon"><Icon Name="lock" /> SLIP-39 + age wallet backup</h1>
@* The encryption is two layers, and the page used to name only the first. A reader
   who then found payload.age.gpg in their backup had been told about age and not
   about OpenPGP, which reads as an unexplained extra file rather than the second
   lock it is. Both are named here, and the reason is one clause: either one holding
   is enough. *@
<p class="subtitle">
    Secure your BIP-39 wallet with threshold secret-sharing, then two layers of
    encryption: age inside OpenPGP, so a weakness in either one still leaves the
    other standing. Every operation runs on this machine; nothing is sent anywhere.
</p>
@* The airgap warning belongs here, not only on the two pages that handle seeds.
   This is where every visitor to the online demo arrives, and it was the one page
   that said nothing about the network: a reader saw a calm landing page, clicked
   through, and only then learned the machine was connected. The warning is worth
   least at the moment someone is about to type a seed and most before they have
   decided to. Owner still takes the callback, because it gates the watermark. *@
<ConnectivityBanner />

<p class="hint-loud">
    Running on Tails, fully offline, is required for a real backup, not advised.
</p>

<div class="choice-pair">
    <div class="panel">
        <div class="panel-body">
            <h2 class="with-icon"><Icon Name="backup" /> Create backup</h2>
            <p class="hint">
                Enter your seed words, choose a threshold, and the tool produces a single
                dated backup zip containing your SLIP-39 share folders and the
                encrypted <code>payload.age</code> blob.
            </p>
            <a href="/owner" class="btn btn-primary">Start backup →</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
        <div class="panel-body">
            <h2 class="with-icon"><Icon Name="recover" /> Recover wallet</h2>
            <p class="hint">
                Gather threshold-many SLIP-39 mnemonics and the <code>payload.age</code>
                ciphertext, then reconstruct your seed words and passphrase here.
            </p>
            <a href="/recoverer" class="btn">Start recovery →</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<p class="hint" style="margin-top:2rem">
    Source, specification and the manual recovery procedure:
    <a href="https://github.com/PeteSparrowBTC/slip39-backup">the repository</a>.
</p>
